      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f3112cf654cd4491457303f|full_name}:\n1. Open the windows Registry Editor.\n2. Navigate to - [Computer\\HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\GraphicsDrivers]\n3. Create a new [DWORD 32 bit value] with the name [TdrDelay].\n4. Set it to a value of [6] with base of [Decimal]. If you are curious the default for this key is [2] which is why we make the time higher for it to recover in more situations.\n5. Restart your computer. \nNow anytime vrchat freezes the GPU should be able to recover after a few seconds. Be prepared for the vr screen to freeze though as that can still be quite disorienting while you wait for it to recover.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-08-10T09:41:47.587Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hello, \nsince weeks the game screen freezes randomly after a small amount of time, mostly half hour to an hour before it happens. I have no issues, the game runs smooth but then out of nowhere the screen freezes for a half second and then you can't interact with it anymore but i still can talk and hear people's voices fine. Also Oculus still works completely fine after that. This is very annoying when you watch Movies.. I already cleared my game cache, verified game files, reinstalled it, reseted Oculus and everything possible but it still keeps happening no matter what world or avatar i use. This didn't happen in over a year of using Oculus, just now. I hope this can be fixed in any way, thanks.",
